OL,3,GNEWSAThe penguins are noisy, the people
OL,4,Afantastic - what it takes to be an
OL,5,AAntarctic postmaster
OL,6,
OL,7,FIt is hardly a typical round for a
OL,8,Fpostie, but for five months of the year
OL,9,FGeorge Clarke leaves behind his partner
OL,10,Fand friends in Bristol to become a
OL,11,Fpostmaster at the world's most
OL,12,Fsoutherly post office - in Antarctica.
OL,14,F"I thought it sounded like an amazing
OL,15,Fexperience - living away from home for
OL,16,Fa few months on a very small island
OL,17,Fwith five other people and 1,000
OL,18,Fpenguins," says Clarke.
OL,20,FHe takes up his role as Port Lockroy
OL,21,Fpostmaster from late October to March,
OL,22,Fduring the southern hemisphere summer.
OL,23,APub: 25-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
